{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:ovs-normal-finite-support-rates",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(X\\) has fixed finite support and every support mass is bounded below.  Use training-cell averages for every OVS-retained propensity, regression, and conditional moment in Definitions \\(\\ref{def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal}\\) and \\(\\ref{def:crossfit-estimator}\\).  Under independent fixed-\\(T\\) sampling, global retained-cell overlap, the global conditional fourth-moment envelope, fixed-fold cross-fitting, \\(\\tau_n\\downarrow0\\), and \\(n^{-1/2}/\\tau_n\\to0\\), uniformly over the fixed number of folds,\n\\[\n\\|\\widehat K_{\\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\\ell}-K_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}\\|_{P_X,4,\\mathrm{op}}\n+\\|\\widehat r_{\\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\\ell}-r_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}\\|_{P_X,4}\n=O_P(n^{-1/2}).\n\\tag{37}\n\\]\nAt every support point, thresholding consistently recovers \\(\\operatorname{rank}K_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(x)\\), and\n\\[\n\\|\\widehat\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\\ell}\n-K_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}^\\dagger r_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}\\|_{P_X,4}\n=O_P(n^{-1/2}/\\tau_n).\n\\tag{38}\n\\]\nOn the rank-recovery event the sharper fixed-law rate is \\(O_P(n^{-1/2})\\).  In particular, if \\(\\tau_n=n^{-a}\\) with \\(0<a<1/4\\), the conservative rate in (38) is \\(O_P(n^{-1/2+a})\\), its square is \\(o_P(n^{-1/2})\\), and its product with either root-\\(n\\) cell-average nuisance rate is \\(o_P(n^{-1/2})\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "X",
      "P",
      "n",
      "Khatovs",
      "Kovs",
      "rhatovs",
      "rovs",
      "alphahatovs",
      "taun",
      "folds"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:orthogonal-ovs-normal-signal",
      "def:ovs-normal-projection",
      "def:crossfit-estimator",
      "lem:ovs-orthogonal-normal-signal",
      "ass:iid-fixed-panel",
      "ass:cell-overlap",
