      "ass:rank-threshold-vanishing"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "There are finitely many values of \\(X\\), cells, periods, and OVS rows.  Global overlap and the lower bound on each support mass imply that every training subsample contributing to a cell average has order \\(n\\) observations with probability tending to one.  For a scalar cell variable \\(W\\) with finite second moment, conditional variance and Chebyshev's inequality give\n\\[\n\\widehat E_{-\\ell}[W\\mid G=a,S=s,X=x]\n-E_P[W\\mid G=a,S=s,X=x]=O_P(n^{-1/2}).\n\\tag{39}\n\\]\nThe global conditional fourth-moment envelope applies (39) to increments and to every product needed for a second moment.  Because all index sets are fixed and support masses are bounded below, taking maxima and the \\(L_4(P_X)\\) norm preserves the order.  Thus \\(\\widehat p-p\\), \\(\\widehat m-m\\), and the preliminary target ratios are all \\(O_P(n^{-1/2})\\).\n\nThe orthogonal-signal lemma and clipping show that replacing \\((p,m)\\) by their cell averages changes each signal in \\(L_4(P)\\) by \\(O_P(n^{-1/2})\\), while its conditional mean changes only by \\(O_P(n^{-1})\\).  Expanding\n\\(\\widehat S^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\widehat S^{\\mathrm{OVS}\\prime}-Z^{\\mathrm{OVS}}Z^{\\mathrm{OVS}\\prime}\\) and applying H\\\"older's inequality proves the first term in (37).  The same expansion of \\(\\widehat S^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\widehat\\psi^0-Z^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\psi^0\\) proves the second.  Shared cohort--period cells create off-diagonal terms in these products, but the cell average estimates those cross-products directly; no block-diagonal approximation is used.\n\nFix a support point \\(x\\).  Since the law and support are fixed, the finite set of positive eigenvalues of \\(K_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(x)\\) has a positive minimum, if it is nonempty.  The variational characterization of ordered eigenvalues gives\n\\[\n|\\lambda_j(\\widehat K(x))-\\lambda_j(K(x))|\n\\le\\|\\widehat K(x)-K(x)\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=O_P(n^{-1/2}).\n\\tag{40}\n\\]\nBecause \\(n^{-1/2}/\\tau_n\\to0\\) and \\(\\tau_n\\to0\\), (40) separates every zero eigenvalue from every fixed positive eigenvalue.  A union bound over the finite support and folds proves simultaneous rank recovery.\n\nOn the recovered range, the inverse identity\n\\[\n\\widehat K_R^{-1}-K_R^{-1}\n=\\widehat K_R^{-1}(K_R-\\widehat K_R)K_R^{-1}\n\\]\nand the fixed-law positive eigenvalue minimum give an \\(O_P(n^{-1/2})\\) inverse error.  Combining this with (37) proves the sharper rate following (38).  Without conditioning on recovery, every retained inverse eigenvalue is at most \\(\\tau_n^{-1}\\), so (37) and the triangle inequality give the conservative rate (38).  Substitution of \\(\\tau_n=n^{-a}\\) yields \\(n^{-1/2+a}\\); its square is \\(n^{-1+2a}=o(n^{-1/2})\\) exactly when \\(a<1/4\\), and multiplication by \\(n^{-1/2}\\) is also \\(o(n^{-1/2})\\).  This proves all claims.",
